id: interface/bot-surfaces-v0.1
title: "yawn.bot index and entrance flow contract v0.1"
kind: interface-contract
status: draft-0.1
updated: 2026-09-12
epistemic_status: inferred
epistemic_note: >
  The components, ranking signal, and prompts named here are observed in
  yawn.bot source. The contract they are assembled into is inferred and
  carries no proof.

purpose: >
  Restructure the flow of two yawn.bot surfaces without touching the skin, the
  header, or any container. The index gains the ranking receipt it already had
  the inputs for, and the entrance prompts gain a paged flow in which the page
  is the address.

reuses_without_change:
  chrome: YawnGlobalChrome
  frame: YawnCoordinateFrame
  view: YawnQuestionView
  disclosure: YawnQuestionDisclosure
  compute_press: YawnQuestionCompute
  skin: the existing pixel-heading, cyan-control reference skin
  rule: >
    No new header, breadcrumb, coordinate, or container. Every change happens
    inside components these surfaces already render.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INDEX — yawn.bot/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

index:
  subject: the product
  questions:
    count: 9
    source: src/domain/yawn-mental-model-network.ts
    unchanged: authored text, the accordion, the collapsed default
  ranking:
    ranker: rankIndexQuestions
    signal: recorded opens, from yawn_index_question_counts
    pinned: the first two questions, so the entry point cannot move under measurement
    tie_break: authored order
    receipt_required: true
    defect_fixed: >
      the view's fallback printed "Source order · no numerical ranking receipt
      supplied" on every row of a list that was in fact ranked by measured
      opens. Each question now carries the policy that placed it, the count
      behind it, the tie-break, and what the count does not mean.
    degradation: >
      with no counts available the receipt reads "no opens recorded yet" and
      the authored order stands. A missing count is never a zero ranking.
    limits_always_shown:
      - an open count measures attention, not truth, trust, or whether the answer helped
      - counted once per consented browser session, from no personal capture text
  kept:
    - the "No purpose vector found" indicator
    - the compute press on every question row
  compute_press_rule: >
    The repeated icon is an affordance, not decoration: it compiles the
    question against the cognition axes and opens the lacunae they report
    missing. It is never removed to reduce repetition. Its stateIcon prop is
    reserved for a source-backed state renderer and stays unsupplied while no
    per-question runtime state exists.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENTRANCE — yawn.bot/new
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

new:
  route_owner: interface/new-yawn-v0.1.yawn
  opening_prompt: "What is pulling your attention?"
  entrance_prompts:
    count: 12
    source: src/domain/yawn-entrance-questions.ts
    order: [become, identity, purpose, attention, direction, emotion, relationship, constraint, uncertainty, options, next, proof]
    order_unchanged: true
    first: questions/what-am-i-to-be.yawn
  judgments:
    required_per_prompt: at least one
    shape: [chosen, rejected, differentiator]
    rendered_in: the existing "How is this answer supported?" disclosure
    epistemic_status: inferred
    rule: >
      A judgment is a comparison, never a proof. Each records the rejected
      alternative so the wording stays contestable instead of inherited.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FLOW — PAGINATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

flow:
  model: pagination
  not: columns
  definition: >
    One question per page. Every other question stays reachable as its own
    page rather than collapsing out of the record.
  address_rule: >
    The page travels in the address as ?q=<question id>. Each page is a real
    href, so a position in a sequence stays shareable, the back button means
    what it looks like, and the page can be server-rendered. Never a carousel
    over client-side state, and never query state that cannot be linked to.
  controls:
    strip: numbered links, one per question, current page marked with aria-current
    pager: previous and next, each labelled with the question it leads to, and the position
    minimum_target: 2.75rem
  active_question: opened on arrival, because on a paged flow the question is the page
  availability: opt-in by address; the accordion remains the default on both surfaces
  availability_reason: >
    The twelve-prompt entrance carries behaviour worth keeping — per-prompt
    drafts, switching between prompts, focus return — that three existing tests
    encode. Making the paged flow the default is a separate decision for dave,
    not a side effect of building it.

invariants:
  - no surface introduces a header, breadcrumb, coordinate, or container of its own
  - the page is an address, never hidden state
  - a ranked list carries its receipt; an unranked one says so honestly
  - orientation coverage, claim confidence, and attention counts stay separate
  - an open count never becomes a claim about truth or helpfulness
  - a judgment is a comparison and carries its rejected pole
  - a self-binding answer is never promoted by the ordinary proof ladder
  - the compute press is never removed to reduce visual repetition
  - a missing count degrades to the authored order, never to a zero ranking

proof:
  required:
    - no row of a ranked list states that no ranking receipt was supplied
    - every paged question is reachable at its own address
    - every entrance prompt shows at least one judgment with its rejected pole
    - the default accordion behaviour is unchanged on both surfaces
    - semantic tokens work without color
    - no horizontal overflow at 390 wide
  human_review_required:
    - whether the paged flow should become the default
    - whether arriving at a paged prompt should also select it

boundary:
  canonicalMutationAuthorized: false
  deploymentAuthorized: false
  publicationAuthorized: false
  externalEffectsAuthorized: false

schema_version: yawn.bot.surfaces.v0.1
